working.why:
X is clearly better: it actually works for normal day-to-day use. One shared context saves every change to localStorage, money is stored as signed cents everywhere, and every control traced through to correct state and storage changes. Its real defects are smaller:
- the month-start setting is ignored;
- the seeded savings transfer is filed under Salary, so it inflates income and adds a Salary slice to the spending donut;
- split amounts are awkward to type;
- rollover covers only one month back.

Y breaks the core finance loop:
- new transactions must be positive, so every one counts as income and you cannot record an expense;
- editing any expense silently turns it into income;
- Mark paid throws an error for every bill;
- the next due date never advances after marking paid;
- budget rollover adds up past limits without subtracting spending;
- the nav bar appears twice on every page;
- the transactions table shows raw account ids and always formats in USD.

Y's only edge is that it applies the month-start setting to budgets.
